-## Git Workflow (MANDATORY — follow automatically every time)
-
-**NEVER commit or push to `master` directly. ALWAYS create a feature branch first.**
-
-### Automatic steps (do these without being asked):
-
-**1. Before ANY task** — pull master:
-```bash
-git checkout master && git pull origin master
-git checkout -b feature/short-task-name
-```
-
-**2. When done** — commit, push, create PR:
-```bash
-git add <specific files>          # NEVER use "git add ." or "git add -A"
-git commit -m "feat: what was done"
-git push -u origin feature/short-task-name
-gh pr create --title "feat: what was done" --body "Summary of changes"
-```
-
-**3. After creating PR** — review diff and merge:
-```bash
-gh pr diff                        # check changes look correct
-gh pr merge --merge               # merge into master
-git checkout master && git pull origin master
-```
-
-Branch naming: `feature/`, `fix/`, `docs/` + short description.
-Never deploy from a feature branch — only from master after PR merge.
-
-## Deployment
-See CLAUDE.md for full deploy script. Server: 192.168.33.3, PM2 on port 3001.
-Secrets in `.env.shared`. Deploy helpers (`_deploy.py`, `_run.py`) are in .gitignore — recreate from CLAUDE.md.
+## Git and Deployment
+Commit only the files you changed (`git add <specific files>`), with a Russian commit message.
+Deployment runs from GitHub Actions on every push to `master` (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`); see AGENTS.md -> Deployment.
